      "writtenOn": "2024-07-10T10:50:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think if we want to optimize further, it might make sense to adjust to use 29 bits for format and 2-3 bits for sample count. 29 bits can hold 536870912 values (max is 0x1FFF_FFFF), should be extensively enough. I have just noticed that currently sample count occupies 15-16 bits in the key, it seems to be very wasteful. Dawn only supports 4 samples, and even 16 samples only need 4 bits to represent (as 15).\n\nFurthermore, even if Dawn changes the enums again, we can place some static_assert here to guard against breakages.\n\nOtherwise, I guess the time we need to query for pipelines is not very frequent, so linear search or hash table should be enough?",
      "parentUuid": "f8eae71b_60cee024",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 842,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 853,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "9b253eded2ff793d1aa0d20887453ee99bc845e7",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2cfba226_955c5cdd",
