      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-10T13:31:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If there is a constant exported along with `wgpu::TextureFormat` like `kLast` or `kTextureFormatCount` that we can use in a static assert, then I would be in favor of trying this approach. The static assert should do a better job catching any such changes much sooner than the SkASSERT did.\n\nI think it would be good to use 4 bits. MSAA16 is not terribly uncommonly available, but MSAA32 is probably something we will ever want to enable. If we need more bits, I wonder if we actually need both sample counts since the color attachment and depth attachment should have the same sample count.",
      "parentUuid": "7ee55956_ce9e5ce9",
